[00:00] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: Creator holding the Amaran Mic, introducing its wireless capabilities.
AUDIO: 'What if you could combine the convenience of a wireless lav mic with the sound quality of a podcast microphone? Well, that is essentially what Amarind has done with their new mic. This works both wired and wirelessly and connects directly to your'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'phone or computer without an audio interface. It has 60 hours of battery life and includes built-in controls and noise reduction. So, in this video, I\'m going to test how this microphone sounds, as well as compare it to some'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'other microphones and show you a few creative ways to use it. &gt;&gt; You got to just press record. &gt;&gt; Let\'s start off by showing what comes included with this mic. You get the microphone itself as well as a desktop stand, the wireless receiver, a USBC'

[00:38] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: Close-up of the Amaran Mic on its stand, showing the control dial and LEDs.
AUDIO: 'cable for charging, as well as directly connecting to your computer. You get this USBC to USBA adapter, and this little handy tool if you want to remove the microphone from the base. In terms'

[00:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of its build quality, the microphone itself is built out of a lightweight plastic, but the arm and base are pretty heavy and help keep it from moving around. So, if you tap the microphone, it\'s not going to fall over. And on the'

[01:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'bottom of the mic, you have a USBC port and a headphone jack. The microphone itself can just swivel on this little arm, and there is no tightening mechanism. Basically, you just move it and it stays there, and you just reposition again. So, you don\'t have to'

[01:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'bother with tightening up the microphone. And on the side of this arm is a little slot that you can actually store away your receiver when not in use, which is pretty handy. Setting up this microphone is really straightforward. Simply take the'

[01:28] [scene:setup]
VISUAL: Creator explaining the setup process, with the Amaran Mic on his desk.
AUDIO: 'receiver and plug it into your device that you are recording to. If that\'s your computer, your phone, or in my case, I\'m actually just plugged into the back of the Osmo Pocket 4P for this angle right here. Your device is going'

[01:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to instantly recognize the microphone of choice. You don\'t have to worry about an audio interface or installing any weird plugins. It\'s just pretty easy and straightforward. As far as the physical controls on the microphone itself, we have two buttons. There is this main'

[01:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'control dial by pressing and holding that will actually turn on the microphone. Once your microphone is connected to your device, it should glow green. And this is your microphone gain input dial. So, I can actually control'

[02:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'how loud or how quiet I want this microphone to be just by rotating this dial. And if you want to control the volume of your headphones, all you got to do is press this button in and it will turn blue. And here I go. I can'

[02:17] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Close-up on the Amaran Mic's controls, demonstrating the gain dial and mute button.
AUDIO: 'control the volume of my headphones. Right above that, we have this little switch that functions both as a mute switch. I can press it right. Press it back and you should hear me. Now, if you press and hold down this'

[02:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'part, it will actually enable noise cancellation. So, this is the light noise cancellation that shows up as a white icon. I can press and hold it again and it\'ll cycle to its stronger noise reduction setting. Press and hold'

[02:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that once more and I return to noise cancellation off. In my opinion, these controls just take a little bit of getting used to, but once you spend a few minutes, it\'s fairly straightforward. Now, in terms of the audio quality, you\'ve been listening to'

[02:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the amaran mic this whole time, and I just have it on this little desk mount. As you can see, it gets it, you know, pretty much in the right position if you are just recording at your desk. What I did notice about this mic, if you talk directly into it, it does pick up on'

