AUDIO: 'in the receiver directly into your phone and there\'s nothing else I had to do. It was that simple. you\'re up and running. I think this has the same convenience of a wireless lav mic, but I would argue that this sounds much better because'

[10:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'obviously it\'s a little bit bigger of a microphone, but they can fit a bigger capsule. You can have better battery life, and it just sounds much richer than those wireless lav solutions. And for reference, this is what the DJI Mic'

[10:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Mini sounds like, just clipped to my shirt. This is a very popular solution and what you might expect to hear from a microphone like this. Or you could use something like this little reporter handle. This is what the DJI Mic Mini'

[11:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'sounds like in the reporter handle. Check. One, two, three, four. Check. One, two, three, 4. Now, a few things to note about the wireless receiver on the side of the phone. There is a USBC port on the side, so you can actually pass'

[11:24] [scene:mobile_use]
VISUAL: Creator speaking into the Amaran Mic, recorded vertically on a smartphone.
AUDIO: 'through charge your phone as you are using the mic, which I\'m glad that they thought out. Another thing I noticed is that the receiver is a little bit too shallow for my phone case because it\'s pretty thick at the bottom. So, it'

[11:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'actually wouldn\'t fit. So, I had to take it off in order to use this microphone. So, that\'s something to keep in mind if you have a phone case like mine. This is made by Nomad. So, you might have to get a different case, particularly with this microphone. But overall, this microphone'

[11:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'feels really simple and I love the way it sounds for a lot of social media use. You could just kind of have it in the frame. If you\'re doing a lot of Instagram, Tik Toks, just kind of getting your message out there. I think this is a great little solution. Plus,'

[12:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it is totally wireless. So, if I want to quickly change my setup, I totally could. Okay, so let\'s talk about a few pros and cons with the amaran mic, as well as what you can expect for the price. Speaking of price, this comes at'

[12:14] [scene:pros]
VISUAL: Creator discussing pros of the Amaran Mic.
AUDIO: '$99 for this kit, which is definitely the more affordable side when it comes to microphones. [music] Not as cheap as something as the Fifine, which is around $60. And of course, this can work with an XLR output to the'

[12:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'computer, whereas this is purely a USBC microphone, but also does make that extremely simple if you are looking to connect to your computer, to your phone, or even a USBC device like your Osmo Pocket 4P or Luna. I also like that it'

[12:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'works both wired and wirelessly. So, even if you just want to have your setup locked down and never worry about battery life or connection issues, it\'s cool that you have the ability just to run a USBC cable directly into it. I'

[12:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'think sound quality is probably the major improvement, especially over something like a wireless lav mic because you\'re getting a much bigger capsule. You are going to get a much richer and deeper sound, which is great if you\'re doing a lot of social media'

[13:08] [scene:cons]
VISUAL: Creator discussing cons of the Amaran Mic.
AUDIO: 'content, but don\'t want to spend a lot on a complicated setup and interface. [music] It\'s really simple just to be able to grab this mic, plug in the receiver to your phone, and you\'re good to go. And even this being a wireless mic, I really'

[13:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'never had an issue with the connectivity of that USB receiver, as well as just connecting to my devices. It all works pretty seamlessly, which is just great. Now, touching on a few downsides of this microphone. Number one, I think the'

[13:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'handling noise is a little bit of a bummer when you think of this as a wireless mic. There are times where I just want to grab this and kind of go handheld with it. and you could, but you just risk getting more of that handheld noise coming through your audio. I also'

[13:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'don\'t like the physical controls. I think they\'re just a little bit too complicated for a complete beginner, as well as they do make more noise when you press it in, which is, you know, really unfortunate. I suppose there is a'

[13:58] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Close-up of the Amaran Mic's control dial and noise cancellation icon.
AUDIO: 'workaround just by using the Amaran app to control the microphone, which could help eliminate that issue. And for me, in terms of just the aesthetics, I\'m not a fan of having LED lights on my microphone. I\'d rather it be discreet.'

[14:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And right now there is no way for me to control turning on or off that light, but maybe you could do that through the Amaran app and have more controls. Another thing I want to point out is the noise reduction modes. So using them is'

[14:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'great. You know, I love the fact that you can enable those on the microphone itself. No matter what device you\'re using, you\'re always going to apply that noise cancellation. The downside is when you do enable that and you are'

[14:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'monitoring with audio, it gets delayed both in the recording as well as just hearing yourself. So it is a little bit annoying when you are trying to let\'s say stream, do a live stream or even on a Zoom call. The fact that you can hear'

[14:47] [scene:mobile_use]
VISUAL: Smartphone recording the creator, with the Amaran Mic receiver attached.
AUDIO: 'yourself echo is unusable in my opinion. So if you\'re going to use those noise reduction modes, I would just recommend taking out your headphones or just not using noise reduction at all. So let\'s talk about who this Amaran microphone is'

[14:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for. Obviously, its big selling point is the fact that it is wireless, which not only makes it a little bit easier to use, but also kind of keeps your setup much cleaner, which is a nice benefit. So, I think this is better suited if you'

[15:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'are doing social media or doing podcast and using your computer or phone to capture your video. I think if you\'re purely going after sound quality, there might be better options for you and forgoing the wireless might be better for you. However, if you do need that'

[15:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'wireless support and just want something very simple and easy to use, for $99, this is a great microphone to get up and running. You know, going into this review, I was wondering if this'

[15:38] [scene:comparison]
VISUAL: Side-by-side view of Fifine AM8, Amaran Mic, and Shure SM7B.
AUDIO: 'microphone could replace all my different microphones, my wireless loaves, my podcast microphones because of its features that it offers. [music] However, after spending some time with it, I don\'t think it necessarily replaces any of those devices. But this'

[15:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is another option if you want something that has a little bit better sound quality than a lav mic, but you don\'t want something as complicated as getting a podcast mic with an interface and plugging that into your phone. If you'

[16:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'want something that is simple but also sounds really good, I think the Amaran mic is just for you. So, that is the new Amaran mic. If you\'re interested in checking out, I\'ll leave a link in the description down below. And if you are building your video setup and need a'

[16:18] [scene:talk]
